course: dictionary
lesson: 11421
title: Knowing someone a little
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Acquainted is a useful word for showing how well people know each other. If you are acquainted with someone, you have met them and know them a little, but they are not a close friend. «Tom and I are acquainted, but we are not best friends.» The words «not best friends» are the clue: acquainted is less than friends.
explain: You can also be acquainted with a thing, such as a book, a rule or a place. «Please get acquainted with the rules before the test.» Here the words «before the test» tell you that getting acquainted means learning about the rules until you know them well enough to use them.
explain: Look at the words around acquainted to find its meaning. «The two girls shook hands and said hello for the first time.» Shaking hands and saying hello for the first time shows they are getting acquainted, which means meeting and starting to know each other.
fact: Acquainted is an adjective, and it is often used after a verb such as be, get or become.
fact: «Acquainted with» means you know a little about a person, a place or a thing.
fact: «Get acquainted» means to meet and start to know each other.
fact: Acquainted is less than friends: you know someone, but not closely.
fact: Acquaint is the verb, and acquainted is also its past form.
exercise: «Lucy and Ben are acquainted, but they are not close friends.» What does acquainted mean here? | They are best friends | They are angry with each other | They have never met | *They know each other a little
exercise: «Please get acquainted with the rules before you play.» What should you do? | *Learn about the rules until you know them | Break the rules on purpose | Forget the rules | Ask someone else to play for you
exercise: Which phrase means to meet and start to know each other? | Left alone | *Get acquainted | Close as sisters | Fast asleep
test: «The new girl and I became acquainted on the first day of school.» What does became acquainted mean? | Moved to a new school | *Met and started to know each other | Forgot each other's names | Lost touch with each other
test: Which word fits the gap? «I am ___ with this book, because I have read it three times.» | *acquainted | famished | curt | dreich
exam: Which sentence shows that two people are only acquainted, not close friends? | Sara and Omar are twins who share a room | Sara and Omar have been best friends since they were babies | *Sara and Omar say hello in the lift, but they hardly know each other well | Sara and Omar tell each other every secret
